# Local planning and test files (not tracked)
PLAN-LDES-EXTENSIONS.md
matlab/test_des_forkjoin.m
python/test-output.txt

.gemini/
gha-creds-*.json

# MATLAB Coder MEX codegen build artifacts (generated)
**/codegen/mex/

# Startup-folder Java classpath override. MATLAB reads a javaclasspath.txt from
# the startup folder as well as from prefdir, and the startup-folder entries
# PRECEDE the prefdir ones, which is how a worktree points MATLAB at its own
# common/jline.jar without editing the shared global file. The paths are
# absolute and machine-specific, so the file must stay out of the repository.
matlab/javaclasspath.txt

# Session scratch space: probes, dumps, and C++ build output. Never tracked --
# a bare `git add -A` once swept 191M of it, including two 90M line-cli binaries.
.scratch/

# Session probe scripts and their dumps. Same hazard as .scratch/ above: these
# are throwaway reproductions left beside the code they probe, and a `git add -A`
# sweep once committed 38 of them. The prefixes are the conventions in use --
# tmp_* beside a MATLAB entry point, zz_* beside a parity runner.
tmp_scratch/
matlab/tmp_*
parity-static/zz_*
parity-static/zzjson/

# jqwik's property-test state, rewritten by every `mvn test` that runs one.
jar/.jqwik-database

# Per-class (tests, seconds) table behind the jar/test_progress.sh meter,
# rewritten from the Surefire XML after every full run. Machine-specific timings.
jar/.test-timings

# Fortran unit 6 written into the cwd when a MATLAB example calls a MEX built
# from Fortran (the layeredModel examples do).
fort.6

# Session probe scripts written beside the MATLAB tree, and the golden snapshots
# taken before a rebase. 553 of these once sat in `git status` at one time,
# burying the real working set. A handful of probes here ARE tracked (the mam_*
# and bgchain checks); a .gitignore rule does not untrack them, so they keep
# showing up in diffs while everything new stays out.
matlab/scratch/

# Per-phase logs of the parallel test driver. The single-file log next to it
# (test_run_*.txt, above) was already ignored; the directory form was not.
test_run_*_parallel/

# Editor and lqns backup copies.
*~

# lqns/lqsim write their .lqxo result beside the model they were handed, so a
# MATLAB layered example leaves one in the examples tree. The .lqxo files under
# jar/src/test/resources are tracked GOLDENS and deliberately not matched here.
matlab/examples/**/*.lqxo

# _kb changelog removed 2026-08-18 as write-only; do not let any worktree re-add it
_kb/log.md

# Octave dumps its session workspace here when a script is run under Octave
# from the repo root. It is a binary session artifact, never an input.
octave-workspace

# Staging copy of the tree that the release scripts assemble (common/, jar/,
# matlab/, python/ mirrored under it). Ignore the STAGING DIR, not release/
# itself -- release.sh, pre-release.sh, github-rsynch.sh and CHANGELOG.textile
# are tracked and live beside it, so a blanket `release/` rule would hide them.
release/line-solver/

# Per-case output of the chaos runs (77 b*_{matlab,python,model,meta}.json for
# SolverBA alone). github-rsynch.sh already excludes chaos/ from a release, but
# git still offered the results as pending work. Matched by RESULTS DIRECTORY so
# that chaos tooling itself (orchestrate.py, which matlab_guard.sh calls) stays
# visible if it is ever added to the tree.
chaos/results_*/

# javac @argfile dumps, written beside the module when a compile spills its
# command line (jar/javac.<timestamp>.args). Regenerated per invocation.
jar/javac.*.args
